    "images": [],
    "text": "Work with us Good IT people, wanted. We're a small, locally-owned IT company in Ludlow. We support businesses properly, not from a call centre, not by closing tickets on a quota. If that sounds like what you're looking for, read on. We're not always hiring, but we're always interested in talking to good engineers. If there's no role open below, send a note to hello@fresh-tech.uk anyway. Send a speculative application → Ludlow Based in Shropshire since 2014 0 No open roles right now Small Team, everyone knows what everyone is doing Why work here What makes us different to work for Small team, real responsibility We're not a call centre. Every engineer owns their client relationships. You'll talk to the same businesses regularly and actually know their setups. Based in Ludlow Proper market town. Not a commute into Birmingham. The role involves some field work across Shropshire, so you'll see a lot of good countryside between calls. No ticket-queue culture We don't measure engineers on tickets closed. We measure on client satisfaction. If fixing something properly takes longer, it takes longer. Good kit, sensible tools You'll have the tools to do the job properly: RMM, PSA, M365 admin, proper documentation. No fighting legacy systems. SJ From Sam, Founder \"I started Fresh Tech because I wanted to do IT support the right way: local engineers, real accountability, no hiding behind a ticket system. If you're good at the technical side but frustrated by working for companies that treat clients as numbers, we should talk.\" We're a small team so every hire matters. We won't waste your time with a lengthy recruitment process; a call and a practical conversation is all it takes. Open roles No roles open right now We don't have a specific opening at the moment, but good people are always welcome to get in touch. A speculative application to hello@fresh-tech.uk will be read by Sam directly. Get in touch Interested? Say hello. No long forms. Email Sam directly: one paragraph about yourself and what you're looking for. hello@fresh-tech.uk →"
